**Note**: This file is part of the comprehensive style guide. For the complete single source of truth, see `global-style-guide.mdc`.

- Use utility-first classes for rapid UI development.
- Create custom themes using Tailwind's configuration file.
- Utilize `@apply` for reusable styles in your CSS files.
- Text inputs, selects, textareas, and search fields must use a visible `border-[0.25px] border-slate-300`. Do not use `border` (1px), `border-none`, `border-0`, `border-white/50`, or `border-slate-200` on a standalone field. See `input-field-borders.mdc`.

## Custom Colors

- Use custom colors defined in `tailwind.config.ts` without intermediate suffixes (100, 200, etc.).
- Custom colors available: `red`, `green`, `blue`, `pink`, `orange`, `brand`, `light`, `dark`, `navy`, `coral`.
- Apply opacity modifiers with `/` syntax: `bg-blue/10`, `text-red/80`, `border-green/20`.
- For colors with variants (like `light`, `dark`, `coral`, `brand`), use the dash notation: `bg-light-300`, `text-dark-100`, `bg-coral-500`.
- Avoid using standard Tailwind color suffixes (e.g., `blue-100`, `red-800`) for custom colors.

### Examples:
- ✅ `bg-blue/10 text-blue border-blue/20`
- ✅ `bg-green/10 text-green`
- ✅ `bg-light-300 text-light-100`
- ✅ `bg-coral-500 text-white`
- ❌ `bg-blue-100 text-blue-800` (don't use intermediate suffixes for custom colors)
- ❌ `bg-red-500` (use `bg-red` or `bg-red/50` instead)